---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { app, links } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Closed alpha" description="Closed-alpha tester sign-ups for MacDigiPet are open in Discord. Selected testers get the build in small waves; no release date has been set.">
  <div class="wrap narrow page">
    <p class="eyebrow">macOS · Community &amp; closed alpha</p>
    <h1>Join the village.</h1>
    <p>Discord is where MacDigiPet grows: development updates, desktop screenshots, ideas from fellow Digimon fans, and the place where alpha testers are picked. You’re welcome to join just to hang out.</p>
    <div class="row actions"><a class="btn" href={links.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join Discord</a><a class="btn alt" href="/wallpaper">Try the free wallpaper</a></div>

    <h2>Closed-alpha sign-ups are open</h2>
    <p>The first alpha focuses on <strong>Digimon World 1</strong>: raising a partner from an egg, care, evolution, the village and battles on your wallpaper. It goes to a small group of testers first, in waves, then to more people as feedback comes in.</p>
    <p>No build has gone out yet and no release date has been set. Joining Discord or applying doesn’t mean a build is available; timing and supported systems are confirmed there after final checks.</p>

    <h2>Who we’re looking for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A Mac on macOS {app.minMacOS}. Final supported systems are confirmed before access.</li>
      <li>15–30 minutes of focused use on about three days a week, for 14 days.</li>
      <li>Honest feedback about installing, saved progress and everyday stability. No developer skills needed.</li>
      <li>Played or finished Digimon World 1? That’s a plus, not a requirement.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to apply</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Join the Discord community using the button above.</li>
      <li>Read <strong>#tester-info</strong> and apply privately there. Share your Mac model/chip, macOS version, display/Spaces setup, time zone and when you can test. Optionally tell us whether you’ve played Digimon World 1.</li>
      <li>The developer reviews applications and assigns the tester role manually. Testers get private download, feedback and bug-report channels.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="notice">Applying doesn’t reserve a slot or guarantee access or a release date. Testers are picked for hardware coverage and availability, not speed or follower count. Donations never guarantee or prioritise access. Please don’t post serial numbers or account details.</div>

    <h2>What to expect from early builds</h2>
    <p>Early builds will have bugs, and that’s the point of testing them. They need macOS {app.minMacOS}; Apple silicon has been tested most. Saves stay on your Mac. Installation steps are shared with testers alongside the build.</p>
    <p>This website does not collect your email or store a signup. Applications are handled manually in Discord, under Discord’s own account and privacy settings. Please keep personal details out of public messages.</p>

    <h2>Keep the project growing</h2>
    <p>Feedback and bug reports are the most useful thing you can give. If you’d also like to support development time and tools, a voluntary tip on <a href={links.kofi} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ko-fi</a> or <a href={links.saweria} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Saweria</a> is always appreciated, never expected.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
